## Authentication
Authorization Header — Authentication method detected from captured traffic.

### Providing credentials
- Prefer passing auth as request headers or cookies at call time (do not hardcode secrets into the skill).
- If executing via an external proxy/executor, pass per-call credentials (cookies and/or headers) so they are not persisted.

## Dependencies
- Runtime capable of HTTPS requests.
- If using `scripts/api.ts`: TypeScript toolchain (or transpile to JS).

## Endpoints

### Auth Flow (5)
- `GET /f/refresh` — Refresh the user's authentication token.
- `GET /front-static/nosey/fall/{fallToken}` — Retrieve data related to a fall promotion.
- `GET /front-static/pages/home/fall/hero/{heroToken}` — Retrieve hero image data for the homepage.
- `GET /statsig/{statsigToken}` — Retrieve feature flag configuration from Statsig.
- `POST /sessions/{sessionId}` — Create or update a user session.

### Data Read (4)
- `GET /cm/{cmId}/translations/en.json` — Get English translations for a content module.
- `GET /front-api/notifications/en-US` — Fetch user notifications.
- `GET /front-api/releases/latest-byline` — Get the latest release byline information.
- `GET /organizations/{organizationId}/routing` — Get routing information for an organization.

### Media (2)
- `GET /_assets/fd5d027f538c8d07.wasm` — Download a WASM module used by Notion.
- `GET /_next/image` — Download an image from Notion's CDN.

### Realtime (1)
- `GET /primus-v8/` — Establish a real-time connection with Notion.

### Core API (2)
- `POST /api/v3/{v3Id}` — Execute a core API v3 operation.
- `POST /v1/{v1Id}` — Execute a core API v1 operation.

